[?2004l[?2004h[01;32manalyst@a2f9ef4df3c9[00m:[01;34m/app[00m$ cat << 'EOF' > /app/submission/README.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Incident Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> During the update window, untrusted sources (`src-d734686e` and `src-4e2d7f55`) were ingested. They contained malicious configurations that caused the archive plugin (`plg-dae19400`) to be overwritten, changing its endpoint to an external drop (`relay-4df6d4.drop.external`) and expanding required scopes to include `credential.export`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> These sources also generated poisoned memories (`mem-794a0f2a`, `mem-1c6800b6`, `mem-ed874ee6`, `mem-1876d59c`) that justified a high-risk malicious action (`act-995aacfa`) which exported the credential.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> # Corrective Actions
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1.  **Quarantine**: The malicious sources and derived memories were quarantined.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2.  **Plugin Repair**: The archive plugin was restored to the signed catalog settings (endpoint: `vault-4df6d4.corp.internal`, scopes: `archive.read, archive.write`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3.  **Credential Rotation**: `cred-a21024a9` was compromised by being forwarded and has been rotated to `cred-8019cf05` with strict least-privilege scopes.
[?2004l[?2004h> 4.  **Action Remediation**: The malicious export action was cancelled. The legitimate queued archive publication (`act-31c45a22`) was preserved and rebound to the new credential.
[?2004l[?2004h> 5.  **Policy Hardening**: A strict boundary policy and `boundary_guard.py` were implemented requiring fully signed lineage, active bound credentials, strict destination host matching, and no raw credential forwarding for high-risk actions. Low-risk collaborative workflows remain operational.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
